{
  "case_id": "2009-08-645",
  "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Hague Convention exists to ensure that custody disputes are resolved by the courts of the country of habitual residence rather than through abduction. It thus generally requires the return of a child who is abducted in violation of a right of custody."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: How many --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: You\u2019re not relying on the order; you\u2019re just relying on the statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ginger Anders",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The ne exeat provision at issue in this case gave Petitioner the power to prevent exactly the harm that is the Hague Convention's central concern."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "why should we include custody to be a situation where the human being who looked at this couple thought that that individual, the husband, should have nothing but visit him occasionally on Christmas? Why should we interpret the word \"custody\" in this treaty to include even that situation, which turns the treaty into a general \u201creturn the child\u201d no matter what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. ANDERS",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0001-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the return remedy is not a determination that the child should live with the left-behind parent or that he should live out the rest of his life in Chile. It's simply a determination that the courts of the country of habitual residence should decide what should happen with the child going forward."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ms. Anders, that's the point, isn't it? The purpose of the convention is which court will decide the life of that child, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. ANDERS",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It says, \"A grave risk that the return would expose the child to physical or psychological harm.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. ANDERS",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the typical case might be one in which a parent with -- with primary physical custody had the child, but the visiting -- the parent with visitation rights took the child to another country. But the fact that it was a typical case means that it wasn't the only type of case, and as -- as family law has developed over the past 30 years, joint rights of custody have become more and more prevalent, and we, therefore, think that this is a joint right to determine residence under the convention, because it gives the father the right to withhold or grant consent to the child's removal from the country."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, suppose there\u2019s a court order that prohibits the -- one of the parents -- the parent with whom the child lives most of the time from moving more than an hour's drive from the prior place of residence, would that be -- would -- would the -- the other parent then have custody?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The focus of the convention was ensuring that the parent who had the primary relationship with -- with the child, that that relationship would not be severed by someone taking a child out of -- of the country. And that was the focus of -- of the convention, which is why there was a distinct difference drawn between protecting rights of access and protecting rights of -- rights of custody."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I don't want to belabor the point too much, but maybe you could just give me an example of a court order that you believe would give a parent the right to determine place of residence and, therefore, would constitute custody within the meaning of the convention."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Not according to the -- what is it, the Chilean central authority, you know, the letter that was sent to the Second Circuit, I think in the Duran case. The -- the authority within Chile that is responsible for the implementation of this Hague Convention said that it regarded that statute to create a custody right for purposes of the Hague Convention."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: So if I -- if I think, as Justice Alito was starting out, that if the -- a court order in the divorce case says the father and mother will jointly decide what house to live in, that the father has a custody right, if it jointly says the father and the mother will decide what State to live in, that that's a custody right. That it says that the father and mother will decide what city, same. The father and mother will jointly what country to live in, same. But suppose that there is no such decree; rather, the jurisdictional statutes of the nation, without considering this family, have a rule that says they have to live in Chile without Court permission. Is there any way I can draw a line, in terms of this statute, between the two situations, the one being where the divorce judge actually focused on the needs and circumstances of a family, the other being where there was no more than a jurisdictional law in a nation that tried to protect the jurisdiction of its courts?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that this does not give any sort of affirmative right to the father, and it is not a right to determine because, if you take the common usage of the right to determine, it is to make an affirmative decision, and --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4252ced49a05b56390cc2b42a2bb33e56610eb9dd24a84438800219a8c87a17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4252ced49a0-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- the United States and Canada -- as we point out in our brief, and I believe that it's pointed out in other amicus briefs, the -- there have only been seven courts of last resort that have heard this issue. There are some 81 countries that belong to the Hague Convention."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-645",
      "confidence": 0.0,
